flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the belt<br/>inner drive face and outer face for cracking or cord<br/>exposure. 2. Check both pulley faces for grooving,<br/>glazing, or material buildup. 3. Inspect the<br/>tensioner body for cracking or seized pivot."]
    box_2{"Severe belt damage, cracking, fraying or<br/>delamination?"}
    box_3(["End, Replace belt: structural failure detected"])
    box_4["Touch a vibration meter probe against the belt at<br/>the midspan position between the two nearest support<br/>pulleys. Pluck the belt lightly perpendicular to the<br/>run and read the natural frequency from the meter<br/>display. Convert the frequency to belt tension using<br/>the conversion formula for the belt mass per unit<br/>length and span length; compare against the target<br/>tension range in the belt drive specification."]
    box_5[/"Refer to the belt tension specification."/]
    box_6{"Belt tension within specified frequency range?"}
    box_7["Adjust belt tension via tensioner bolt to<br/>specification"]
    box_8{"Reverify belt tension after adjustment"}
    box_9(["End, Escalate: tensioner mechanism worn, replace"])
    box_10["Place a long straight edge across the faces of both<br/>pulleys in the same plane, resting on the highest<br/>point of each pulley face. Use feeler gauges to<br/>check the gap between the straight edge and each<br/>pulley face at both ends of the straight edge. A gap<br/>on one pulley indicates angular or axial<br/>misalignment; record the maximum gap dimension and<br/>the location."]
    box_11{"Belt tracking aligned, no lateral drift?"}
    box_12["Adjust pulley alignment, loosen and retorque<br/>mounting"]
    box_13["Spin each pulley by hand and observe the running<br/>surface for wobble, which indicates hub or bore<br/>wear. Mount a dial test indicator against the pulley<br/>rim and rotate slowly through one full revolution to<br/>measure radial runout. Inspect the belt contact<br/>surface for ridges, corrosion, or material transfer<br/>from the belt that could cause uneven belt wear."]
    box_14{"Pulley runout within 0.05 mm total indicator<br/>reading?"}
    box_15["Replace worn pulley or remachine flange"]
    box_16["Using a vernier caliper with a depth blade, measure<br/>the groove depth at three circumferential positions<br/>on each pulley that contacts the belt. Record the<br/>minimum groove depth and compare against the minimum<br/>serviceable depth in the drive specification.<br/>Inspect the belt edges for cracking, fraying, or<br/>cord exposure that would indicate belt replacement<br/>is required regardless of tension."]
    box_17[/"Refer to the belt wear limit table."/]
    box_18{"Belt wear within remaining service life limit?"}
    box_19["Replace belt and reset service interval counter"]
    box_20["Complete the following checks: 1. Run the drive<br/>under load for five minutes and check for abnormal<br/>heat radiation. 2. Listen for squealing, rumbling,<br/>or slapping noise from the belt drive. 3. Check<br/>pulley alignment with a straight edge across both<br/>pulley faces."]
    box_21{"No abnormal noise or temperature rise observed?"}
    box_22["Log belt service data and update maintenance<br/>management system"]
    box_23(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_24["Secondary tension correction: release the tensioner<br/>adjustment screw completely and retension the belt<br/>from zero load using the vibration frequency method<br/>to set the correct natural frequency incrementally.<br/>Verify pulley alignment with the straight edge after<br/>retensioning to confirm that adjustment has not<br/>introduced misalignment before returning to the belt<br/>tension measurement step."]
    box_25[/"Belt conveyor tracking diagnostic (GRAPH 36)"/]

